==diff
jj diff = jj diff -r @
jj diff -r rev = jj diff -f rev- -t rev
jj diff -r rev- -r rev = jj diff -f rev- -t rev
* can use rev- and rev+, rev--, rev++
* can not use -r rev-2, have to use -r 'parents(@, 3)'
example: jj log -r "parents(@, 3) | parents(@, 1)" -p
* since there is only linear history, there is no ~ and ^

==log
show log first parent to debug diffs: jj log -r "parents(@, 2) | parents(@, 1)" -p
templating: jj log -r "parents(@, 2) | parents(@, 1)" --template "change_id.short() + ' ' + description.first_line() + '\n'"
* There is no way to do formatted output of logs, but one can use revset-aliases as workarounds.
& { jj log -r "parents(@, 2) | parents(@, 1)"; echo "----"; jj log -r "parents(@, 2) | parents(@, 1)" -p }
[revset-aliases]
# Defines a custom function 'p(from, to)' that evaluates parents dynamically
'p(from, to)' = 'parents(@, from) | parents(@, to)'
& { jj log -r "p(2, 1)" ; echo "----"; jj log -r "p(2, 1)" -p }

